So let's think about it.

00:15:05.140 --> 00:15:14.860
Collectively, all the
sequences with this property,

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:26.260
so collectively, their
probability is essentially 1

00:15:26.260 --> 00:15:29.320
because I said we talked about
how with high probability,

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:31.930
the law of large numbers tells
us that with high probability,

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:35.920
with all likelihood, in
other words with probability

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:41.230
essentially 1, the sequence
that we're going to get

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:42.685
is going to have this property.

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:52.260
So collectively, all the
sequences with this property

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:58.410
have probability about
1, and each of them,

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:01.530
by definition of
this property, each

00:16:01.530 --> 00:16:08.130
of these has this probability.

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:14.670
Has probability approximately
2 to the minus nh.

00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:28.810
So how many such sequences
are there approximately?

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:37.580
We've got a collection of
